# Type-specific templates workflow

`pebbles new` prompts for type-specific template fields when creating
interactively (stdin is a terminal) and stores the answers as metadata on
the new issue (r[type-templates]). When stdin is not a terminal - piped
and scripted creates, like the trycmd harness - the fields are skipped:
no prompt text is printed, nothing is read from stdin, and the create
never blocks. This workflow exercises the non-interactive path.

## Create a bug from piped stdin does not prompt or block

The bug template fields (`expected`, `actual`) are skipped: the create
prints exactly the usual output with no prompt lines, and completes
without reading stdin (a blocking read would hang this harness).

r[verify type-templates]
```console
$ pebbles new "Crash on login" --issue-type bug
Created bug [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Crash on login
Type: Bug
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: bug-[..]-crash-on-login.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

```

No template metadata was stored by the piped create: the `expected` and
`actual` keys were skipped, so the metadata filters match nothing.

```console
$ pebbles list --metadata expected=
No issues found.

```
```console
$ pebbles list --metadata actual=
No issues found.

```

## Create a ux_problem from piped stdin

The ux_problem template (`before_screenshot`, `after_screenshot`) is
likewise skipped when stdin is not a terminal.

```console
$ pebbles new "Onboarding header cut off" --issue-type ux_problem
Created ux_problem [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Onboarding header cut off
Type: UxProblem
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: ux-[..]-onboarding-header-cut-off.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

```
```console
$ pebbles list --metadata before_screenshot=
No issues found.

```
```console
$ pebbles list --metadata after_screenshot=
No issues found.

```

## Create a usecase from piped stdin

The usecase template (`acceptance_criteria`) is skipped too.

```console
$ pebbles new "Export to CSV" --issue-type usecase
Created usecase [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Export to CSV
Type: Usecase
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: uc-[..]-export-to-csv.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

```
```console
$ pebbles list --metadata acceptance_criteria=
No issues found.

```

## All three created issues exist

Each piped create did create the issue (with no template metadata).

```console
$ pebbles list --issue-type bug
[..] [bug] [PROPOSED] Crash on login ✓

```
```console
$ pebbles list --issue-type ux_problem
[..] [ux] [PROPOSED] Onboarding header cut off ✓

```
```console
$ pebbles list --issue-type usecase
[..] [uc] [PROPOSED] Export to CSV ✓

```
